  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 217 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nAs the upper ridge begins to move our way in earnest and SSWly flow \nramps up, we will once again see a strong warming trend to near \nrecord summer heat. Highs Sunday through at least Tuesday reach 100 \nacross nearly the entire area with Heat Index values up to 110. The \nNWS HeatRisk tool shows the entire forecast area in Major to Extreme \nfor early next week, with some areas in the west only cooling to \naround 80 overnight.\n\nOnce precipitation Friday night comes to end end throughout \nSaturday morning, additional precipitation is not expected for \nthe rest of the forecast period. Long term outlooks indicate \nbest chances for near-normal temperatures and precipitation to \nstart August, which would put highs around 90 and up to an inch \nof rain in a seven day period. While the ridge looks to stick \naround for a while, it appears we may be lucky to remain close \nenough to the periphery to benefit from some stray energy for \nprecipitation.",
